# Architecture Overview

**Status:** Living document | **Last reviewed:** 2026-11-07

## Goals and non-goals

**Goals:** correctness of business data, tenant isolation, operability by a small team, fast iteration, predictable cost.

**Non-goals (for now):** multi-region active-active, microservices, event sourcing. We deliberately start as a **modular monolith**; split only when a measured problem demands it.

## System context

{% if project_type == 'full-stack' %}
```
 Browser --HTTPS--> CDN / Edge --> Frontend (static SPA, FSD)
    |
    +--HTTPS /api/v1--> API service --> Data store (system of record)
                              |   |
                              |   +--enqueue--> Job queue --> Workers
                              |
                              +--> Identity Provider
```

The API and the workers share one backend package and its domain code, but
deploy as separate processes so they scale independently.
{% elif project_type == 'frontend-only' %}
```
 Browser --HTTPS--> CDN / Edge --> Frontend (static SPA, FSD)
                                       |
                                       +--HTTPS /api/v1--> API service (owned by another repository)
                                       +--> Identity Provider (owned by the API repository)
```

This repository ships only the frontend. The API, its database, and its jobs
live in the service it calls. The contract between them is the OpenAPI schema,
regenerated with `{{ api_client_command }}`; a breaking change there is a
cross-repository event, not a local refactor.
{% else %}
```
 Clients --HTTPS /api/v1--> API service --> Data store (system of record)
                                  |   |
                                  |   +--enqueue--> Job queue --> Workers
                                  |
                                  +--> Identity Provider
```

This repository ships only the backend. Its browser clients are built and
deployed separately and consume the OpenAPI schema this service publishes.
{% endif %}

