## Non-functional targets (initial SLOs)

| Concern | Target |
|---|---|
{% if backend %}
| API availability | 99.9% monthly |
| API latency | p95 < 300 ms, p99 < 1 s (excluding exports/reports) |
| Job latency | 95% of jobs start within 30 s of enqueue |
| RPO / RTO | RPO <= 5 min, RTO <= 1 h |
| Data durability | Daily backups + point-in-time recovery, restore tested quarterly |
{% endif %}
{% if frontend %}
| Initial JS | <= 200 KB gzipped on the main route |
| LCP / INP / CLS | < 2.5 s / < 200 ms / < 0.1 |
| Accessibility | WCAG 2.2 AA |
{% endif %}

## Observability

{% if backend %}
- **Logs:** structured JSON, no PII or secrets.
- **Metrics:** rate, errors, and duration per route; queue depth, age, and failure rate per task.
- **Traces:** OpenTelemetry across API, database, workers, and outbound calls.
- **Alerts:** symptom-based (SLO burn). Every alert links to a runbook.
{% endif %}
{% if frontend %}
- **Client errors:** one error-reporting sink; every report carries the route, release, and request ID.
- **Web vitals:** LCP, INP, and CLS reported per route.
- **Build output:** bundle-size budget checked in CI.
{% endif %}

## Deployment

{% if backend %}
Containerized, immutable images, deployed via CI/CD with automated rollback on failed health checks. Migrations in `{{ migrations_root }}` run before app rollout and must be backward compatible (expand/contract) so rollbacks are safe.
{% endif %}
{% if frontend %}
The frontend is built to static assets and served from a CDN with immutable, content-hashed filenames; the HTML entry is never cached long.
{% endif %}

## Known risks and trade-offs

{% if backend %}
- Module boundaries can erode; mitigated by enforced import contracts in CI.
- Shared-schema tenancy risks cross-tenant leaks; mitigated by row-level security and mandatory tenant-isolation tests.
- A single database primary is a scaling ceiling; mitigated by indexing discipline, read replicas, and caching before sharding.
{% endif %}
{% if frontend %}
- The client is at best a second enforcement point: UX may mirror a business rule, never own it (see `frontend.md`).
- Bundle growth; mitigated by route-level code splitting and the size budget in CI.
{% endif %}
{% if project_type == 'frontend-only' %}
- The API contract can change without this repository noticing; mitigated by regenerating types in CI and failing on drift.
{% endif %}

